    "summary": "Carved wooden bowl, kumete. Rounded rectangular deep bowl: flat-bottomed, with figure supports facing outwards at each end. Both figures with wheku faces, unsexed; haliotis-shell eyes and three circles of other type of shell on each side of rim and one on each foot of figures; plain bodies, three-fingered hands, with knuckles and nails, on stomach; plain spirals with straight ritorito on thighs, pakura on feet. Band of pakura around rim. Sides of bowl in horizontal whakarare. Very sharp metal cuts.",
